meta {
  name: qnib-ftest
  seq: 5
}

auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{oci_bearer}}
}

vars:pre-request {
  repo: qnib/ftest
  tag: latest
}

docs {
  # qnib-ftest — inspect the qnib/ftest artefacts populated by
  # `metahub-admin parse collections` (pullthrough-repo session).

  ## Auth prerequisite (one-time per session)

  Every request in this folder sends `Authorization: Bearer {{oci_bearer}}`
  (inherited via folder-level `auth:bearer`). To populate `oci_bearer`,
  do ONE of:

    A) Run `qnib-ftest/refreshToken` (seq 0). Single click — performs
       the /v2 WWW-Authenticate challenge AND the /auth token exchange
       inline, then stores `oci_bearer` in the active environment.

    B) Run `auth/get` then `auth/getToken` in order (the classic path).
       Produces the same result.

  Both paths require `username` + `password` in the active environment
  (already set to `oci` / `oci` in `metahub-dev.bru` and
  `metahub-local.bru`).

  ## Request sequence

  After `refreshToken` (seq 0) runs, execute the inspection chain in
  order — each post-response script extracts the variable the next
  step needs:

    0. refreshToken        — mint oci_bearer (single-click auth)
    1. getTagsList         — confirm the Tag is discoverable
    2. headIndexByTag      — HEAD the Slot's computed :Index,
                             content-negotiated as an OCI image-index
                             (regression guard #10)
    3. getIndexByTag       — GET body; post-script extracts
                             `indexDigest` + `childManifestDigest` +
                             `childManifestSize`
    4. getIndexByDigest    — round-trip Index by its own digest
    5. headChildManifest   — HEAD first per-arch manifest; cross-checks
                             Index-descriptor-size vs manifest-body-size
                             (regression guard for metalib aefa27f)
    6. getChildManifest    — GET same; extracts `configDigest` +
                             `firstLayerDigest`
    7. getConfigBlob       — GET image config blob (regression guard
                             for pipeline-repo cab4cf7 bucket alignment)
    8. headLayerBlob       — HEAD first layer blob
    9. neo4jSlotChain      — out-of-band Neo4j Cypher: Slot->HAS_PUSHED
                             ->Manifest + Slot->POINTS_TO->Index counts
                             (mirrors Verify-CE #9)

  The chain mirrors what `manifest-tool inspect <registry>/qnib/ftest:latest`
  performs under the hood. Each step's post-response script raises a
  contextual error if it fails, so "step 4 returned 404" isolates the
  problem immediately.
}
